{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED for task/worktree-visibility at exact head dfa02060c3e3b9f2c0c052150a28ba3491ca47d4. Head verified before and after; probes deleted, worktree clean. Gates green at this head: vet, test, -race, build, ui npm test 14/14. Every finding in 0165735ef0b8a55b4f98a6455f9630a331fe4e75 is closed, and because they were my own findings I checked them by re-running the measurements that produced them rather than by reading the diff and recognising my own words.\n\nThe five must-fixes, each verified by execution against a live resident or the real module:\n\n(1) The index writes are gone. Both git invocations now carry --no-optional-locks. Against a running gs serve over a five-worktree fixture, a real /v0/worktrees request left all four index mtimes at 946702800, unchanged. The doc comment that previously said \"without writing anything to git\" is now true rather than aspirational. The fan-out also gained an 8-second cache, a 10-second poll instead of 5, a 750ms per-worktree and 3s overall timeout, and a 128-worktree ceiling, which closes finding 10 in the same stroke.\n\n(2) The fabricated association is gone. dependsOnAny now stops at any request, promise or report that is not itself an anchor. I reconstructed the exact case from the report — commitment A, an ordinary \"next, do X\" request B resting on A's report, B's artifact, and a checkout of B — and it now returns the empty list where it previously returned that checkout with a green exact-match. I also checked the repair did not close it by narrowing the feature: A's own artifact still associates, with headMatches true and evidence durable.\n\n(3) Current is correct from a subdirectory. Resolution now goes through rev-parse --show-toplevel. Serving with --repo \".\" from main/sub, the toplevel checkout comes back current true and sorts first.\n\n(4) The detached overload is gone. Detached is a separate boolean and Branch is left empty, so in one fixture a genuinely detached worktree reports detached true with no branch while a worktree on a branch literally named detached reports branch detached with no flag — distinguishable, which they were not. The React key moved off branch:checkout, so the basename collision is closed too.\n\n(5) Bare, locked and prunable are parsed and distinct. A bare repository now reports state bare and renders as bare rather than \"unborn @no HEAD\"; a worktree whose directory was deleted reports state prunable, distinct from the unavailable a transient read error produces. It still carries the branch and head git itself reports for that record, which is truthful and now unambiguous because the badge differs.\n\nThe should-fixes: (6) the body.branch/head/commit convention is documented in both SKILL.md and docs/reference.md as advisory hints that do not make cleanliness durable; (7) and (9) trailer-derived rows now carry a visible \"unverified trailer\" marker and every pill carries a visible \"local\" label rather than a hover-only caveat; (8) the graph endpoint reports truncated and the drawer says the window is the newest eighty, with a test that builds 81 commits and asserts both; (11) headMatches no longer goes silent with two declared heads — I confirmed a checkout at neither of two declared heads now comes back headMatches false with both heads listed, where it previously came back undefined; (12) the path-privacy test now checks the linked checkout's path as well as the serving repository's, against a two-worktree fixture, and a new test covers detached, locked, prunable and bare.\n\nI checked what the repair might have opened rather than only what it closed. Path privacy still holds: only basenames leave the boundary, including for a checkout whose directory name contains a space, and the new 128-worktree refusal reports a count and no path. The UI bundle is still reproducible — two builds diffed byte-identical — and the committed bundle matches the branch source, so the generated artifact is not stale. One note rather than a finding: exceeding the 128-worktree ceiling surfaces to the user as \"Local checkout state unavailable\" rather than as the stated limit, which is honest but less informative than the error text deserves.\n\nDisclosure: the original review was swept by a delegate under my direction; this re-review I ran myself end to end."}